t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Today, President Donald J. Trump returns to the Peach State with a proven record of America First results that put Georgia workers, families, seniors, and communities first.</strong> Under the leadership of President Trump and Republicans, Georgians are seeing historic tax relief, a surge of private investment and job creation, lower energy costs, support for farmers, the most secure border in a generation, and safer streets.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-delivering-tax-relief-for-hardworking-georgians\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Delivering Tax Relief for Hardworking Georgians</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump’s Working Families Tax Cuts are putting real money back in the pockets of Georgia workers, families, and seniors.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>No Tax on Social Security:</strong> Approximately 1.8 million Georgia seniors <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Georgia-WH-OBBB-Savings-by-State.pdf\">benefit</a> from the new senior deduction, with the average senior expected to pay zero federal taxes on Social Security benefits.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Bigger Refunds:</strong> Georgia taxpayers saw average refunds of <a href=\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/average-tax-refunds-by-state-county/\">$3,169</a> in 2026.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Protecting Jobs and Wages:</strong> The Working Families Tax Cuts <a href=\"https://nam.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/NAM_Tax_Wins_Collection_Final.pdf#page=12\">safeguarded</a> 198,000 Georgia jobs, $36 billion in state GDP, and $18 billion in workers’ wages.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Rural Health Investments:</strong> Georgia <a href=\"https://scdailygazette.com/2025/12/30/sc-to-receive-200m-in-first-rural-hospital-funding-allocation/\">secured</a> $219 million in first-year Rural Health Transformation Program funding from the Working Families Tax Cuts.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-unleashing-a-private-investment-and-jobs-boom\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Unleashing a Private Investment and Jobs Boom</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump’s pro-growth, America First agenda is driving major private investment and high-quality job creation throughout the Peach State.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Pirelli is <a href=\"https://georgia.org/press-releases/2026/pirelli-invest-12-billion-georgia-expansion\">investing</a> $1.2 billion to expand its Rome facility, creating 1,000 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mayville Engineering Company is <a href=\"https://www.plantservices.com/industry-news/news/55409556/mayville-engineering-company-plans-metal-fabrication-manufacturing-facility-in-georgia\">investing</a> as much as $30 million to establish a new metal fabrication facility in Thomson.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Siemens is <a href=\"https://www.plantservices.com/industry-news/news/55398698/siemens-invests-185-million-to-build-low-voltage-electrical-components-manufacturing-facility-in-georgia\">investing</a> $185 million to build a new advanced manufacturing facility in Pendergrass, creating 1,400 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>DeltaX is <a href=\"https://gov.georgia.gov/press-releases/2026-08-14/gov-kemp-deltax-establish-north-american-hq-walton-county\">investing</a> $141 million to establish its North American manufacturing headquarters in Walton County, creating 250 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>ArcelorMittal Building Solutions is <a href=\"https://gov.georgia.gov/press-releases/2026-06-01/gov-kemp-arcelormittal-building-solutions-brings-north-american-hq-macon\">investing</a> $107 million to build a new manufacturing facility in Macon-Bibb County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rideout Arsenal is <a href=\"https://georgia.org/press-releases/2026/rideout-arsenal-bringing-22m-120-new-jobs-thomas-co\">investing</a> $22 million to build a new manufacturing facility, creating 120 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Yancey Engineered Solutions is <a href=\"https://www.plantservices.com/industry-news/news/55387137/yancey-engineered-solutions-to-build-57-million-georgia-plant\">investing</a> $5.7 million to build a new factory in Cordele, creating 300 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Unified Legacy is <a href=\"https://gov.georgia.gov/press-releases/2026-05-15/georgia-based-unified-legacy-create-500-new-jobs-macon-bibb-county\">investing</a> $125 million to construct a new manufacturing facility in Macon-Bibb County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>UCB is <a href=\"https://www.gwinnettcounty.com/-/news-events/news-releases/news-details/gwinnett-county-announces-2-billion-ucb-manufacturing-facility-at-rowen\">investing</a> $2 billion to build a manufacturing facility in Gwinnett County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pratt &amp; Whitney is <a href=\"https://gov.georgia.gov/press-releases/2026-02-24/rtxs-pratt-whitney-announces-new-200m-columbus-expansion-cuts-ribbon\">investing</a> $200 million to expand operations in Muscogee County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Georgia is also positioned to capture a significant share of GE Appliances’ <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/1955613237380071909\">$3 billion</a> U.S. investment, Thermo Fisher Scientific’s <a href=\"https://ir.thermofisher.com/investors/news-events/news/news-details/2025/Thermo-Fisher-Scientific-Invests-to-Enhance-U-S--Innovation-and-Support-Customers-Manufacturing/default.aspx\">$2 billion</a> U.S. investment, Silver Lake’s <a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/articles/silver-lake-invests-400-million-to-tackle-data-center-power-bottleneck-7850ca17\">$400 million</a> U.S. investment, Anheuser-Busch’s <a href=\"https://www.foxbusiness.com/politics/beer-giant-pours-600m-us-production-major-bet-american-growth\">$300 million</a> U.S. investment, and General Dynamics’ <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-06-01/general-dynamics-will-spend-200-million-to-reboot-ammo-plant?srnd=homepage-americas\">$200 million</a> U.S. investment, among others.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-supporting-georgia-families-farmers-and-communities\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Supporting Georgia Families, Farmers, and Communities</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump is shielding Georgia families from higher costs and delivering support where it is needed most.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Protecting Ratepayers:</strong> Georgia Power is <a href=\"https://www.georgiapower.com/news-hub/press-releases/georgia-psc-approves-plan-to-freeze-base-rates-through-2028.html\">freezing</a> base rates through 2029 and <a href=\"https://www.georgiapower.com/news-hub/press-releases/contract-openai-approved-part-portfolio-delivering-950-million-annual-savings.html\">delivering</a> more than $2.8 billion in savings — $180 per year in savings for the typical residential consumer. Georgia’s major utilities have <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/ratepayer-protection-pledge/\">signed</a> President Trump’s <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/ratepayer-protection-pledge/\">Ratepayer Protection Pledge</a>, ensuring large data centers — not Georgia ratepayers — pay for the power and infrastructure they require.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Delivering for Farmers:</strong> The Trump Administration has delivered <a href=\"https://www.fsa.usda.gov/resources/programs/emergency-commodity-assistance-program/dashboard\">more than $177 million</a> to over 4,300 Georgia farmers through the Emergency Commodity Assistance Program and <a href=\"https://publicdashboards.dl.usda.gov/t/FPAC_PUB/views/FSA-DAFP-FBADashboard/ProgramPaymentsbyCategoryandCommodity?%3Aembed=y&amp;%3AisGuestRedirectFromVizportal=y\">more than $171 million</a> to over 4,000 producers under a <a href=\"https://www.usda.gov/about-usda/news/press-releases/2025/12/08/trump-administration-announces-12-billion-farmer-bridge-payments-american-farmers-impacted-unfair\">$12 billion</a> national bridge program for trade disruptions and higher input costs left by the Biden Administration.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Delivering Disaster Relief:</strong> After Hurricane Helene, President Trump <a href=\"https://www.fema.gov/press-release/20260703/president-donald-j-trump-increases-federal-cost-share-georgia\">raised</a> the federal cost-share for Georgia disaster relief from 75% to 90%, <a href=\"https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/116841674801545467\">approved</a> a $318.3 million Disaster Declaration Request, and <a href=\"https://www.dhs.gov/news/2025/12/12/secretary-noem-announces-1-billion-fema-funding-georgia\">announced</a> more than $1 billion in FEMA funding for communities and healthcare facilities.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-securing-the-border-and-ending-the-biden-era-betrayal\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Securing the Border and Ending the Biden-era Betrayal</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump ended the open borders policies that enabled tragedies like the murder of Laken Riley and restored the most secure border in a generation.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>President Trump <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/1884690966667231272\">signed</a> the Laken Riley Act into law, <a href=\"https://www.foxnews.com/politics/trump-signs-laken-riley-act-law-first-legislative-victory-new-administration\">requiring</a> detention of illegal immigrants charged with theft or violence — honoring the legacy of Laken Riley, a Georgia student murdered by an illegal alien previously released into the country.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/10/16/under-president-trump-and-secretary-mullin-dhs-announces-lowest-fiscal-year-border\">has not released</a> a single illegal alien from the border into the U.S. interior for <a href=\"https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/10/16/under-president-trump-and-secretary-mullin-dhs-announces-lowest-fiscal-year-border\">17 straight months</a>.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refugee admissions are <a href=\"https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/17/refugee-admissions-to-the-us-are-dropping-sharply-in-trumps-second-term/#:~:text=The%20federal%20government%20has%20admitted%2010%2C258%20refugees%20through%20the%20first%2010%20months%20of%20fiscal%20year%202026%2C%20which%20ends%20on%20Sept.%2030.%20That%E2%80%99s%20down%20from%2038%2C102%20refugees%20in%20fiscal%202025%20and%20100%2C034%20in%20fiscal%202024.%20(President%20Joe%20Biden%20was%20in%20office%20for%20part%20of%20fiscal%202025%20and%20all%20of%20fiscal%202024.)\">down</a> nearly 90% from 2024 levels.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Southern border apprehensions in August were <a href=\"https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/09/16/trump-administration-delivers-16-straight-months-zero-releases-border\">94% lower</a> than the monthly average under the Biden Administration.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The U.S. <a href=\"https://abcnews.com/US/us-1st-time-50-years-experienced-negative-net/story?id=129175522\">recorded</a> negative net migration in 2025 for the first time in half a century, with more than three million illegal aliens having <a href=\"https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/01/20/dhs-sets-stage-another-historic-record-breaking-year-under-president-trump\">left</a> the country since President Trump returned to office.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>ICE has <a href=\"https://www.dhs.gov/news/2026/06/24/making-america-safe-again-ice-hits-milestone-more-10000-gang-members-arrested-under\">arrested</a> more than 10,000 gang members during President Trump’s second term.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-making-georgia-s-streets-safer\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Making Georgia’s Streets Safer</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Crime is falling across Georgia as President Trump’s immigration enforcement, support for law enforcement, and tough-on-crime policies Make America Safe Again.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>In Atlanta, murders <a href=\"https://majorcitieschiefs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/MCCA-Violent-Crime-Report-2025-and-2024-Year-End.pdf\">dropped</a> 22% last year and continued plunging in 2026 — with homicides <a href=\"https://majorcitieschiefs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/MCCA-Violent-Crime-Report-2026-and-2025-First-Quarter.pdf\">down</a> 36% in the first quarter compared to last year.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In DeKalb County, murders <a href=\"https://majorcitieschiefs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/MCCA-Violent-Crime-Report-2025-and-2024-Year-End.pdf\">fell</a> nearly 30% last year.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump and Republicans are delivering lower taxes, major private investment, support for ratepayers and farmers, a secure border, and safer communities.</strong> Georgians face a clear choice: continue this progress, or return to the higher taxes, open borders, and failed policies of the past.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/10/president-trump-returns-to-georgia-with-a-record-of-results/\">President Trump Returns to Georgia with a Record of Results</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
